Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:19:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updater: pick the highest harmony version instead of the
 first listed

getLatest() took the first release of the list GetApplicationRelease had
already narrowed to the channel (and, for the update check, to releases newer
than the running build). GitHub does not promise an order and the mirror that
CI writes to the repo branch is the API answer at the time it ran, so a preview
of the last upstream version could sit in front of a newer one and the app kept
offering the older build.

The candidates are now ordered by their (major, minor, patch, harmony) tuple,
newest first; the joined release notes follow that order. Tags that do not
parse sort last. The regex and the comparison move to file level so the
extension function can share them with the class. Adds a unit test with the
newest release listed second.

Harmony-only: same bug and fix as mihon-harmony 0017; Animeko 0002 already
sorts and takes the max.
